{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md | sed -n '45,125p'\"","aggregated_output":"    45\t  argument), so it gains one only by being handed a coordinate-built handle.\n    46\t- **The async facade** (`dao.jing.content.async`): replaces\n    47\t  `dao.jing.remote.async` over the new stepped client, same consumer API;\n    48\t  `dao.data.btree.storage` is the consumer (`hydrate-async`,\n    49\t  `store-tree-async`).\n    50\t- **The coordinate**: `{:dao.jing/type :dao.jing/remote :dao.jing/requests\n    51\t  <remote descriptor> :dao.jing/answers <remote descriptor>}` on every\n    52\t  host, resolved by `dao.jing.coordinate/open!` to the driver on clj and to\n    53\t  the stepped client elsewhere. The `:url` form is gone; its consumers are\n    54\t  the tests and the coordinate itself.\n    55\t\n    56\t## 2. Contract boundary\n    57\t\n    58\tThe `dao.stream.md` changes are the only changes to that contract: OD-1,\n    59\tOD-2 and OD-3; the `:dao.stream/refused` rows on `cursor`, `next` and\n    60\t`append!`; and the composed-handle sentence in Surfaces. They add no network\n    61\tor capability concept. Section 5 holds the fate of every network path;\n    62\tsection 4 lists companion-document edits.\n    63\t\n    64\t## 3. Completion criteria and implementation slices\n    65\t\n    66\tOrdered. Each names files, host lanes and its proof. Verification commands\n    67\tare in `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`.\n    68\t\n    69\t+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\n    70\t| #  | Slice and files                                            | Proves                                                       | Lanes         |\n    71\t+====+============================================================+==============================================================+===============+\n    72\t| 0  | Contract and source alignment: the `dao.stream.md`         | Existing consumers pass; `dao.stream.observe/step` and the   | clj cljs cljd |\n    73\t|    | amendments of the plan's section 2 are accepted;           | engine treat an unrecognized outcome as refused, not a       |               |\n    74\t|    | `:dao.stream/refused` added to the closed outcome sets     | throw; the outcome sets admit the refusal.                   |               |\n    75\t|    | for `cursor`, `next` and `append!` in                      |                                                              |               |\n    76\t|    | `src/cljc/dao/stream.cljc`; `dao.stream.observe`,          |                                                              |               |\n    77\t|    | `yin.vm.engine` follow the unrecognized-outcome rule.      |                                                              |               |\n    78\t+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\n    79\t| 1  | `dao.stream.middleware`: `apply-request`, `wrap`, `gate`,  | Position rule under a value cipher over a ring buffer; a     | clj cljs cljd |\n    80\t|    | `present`, a metering exemplar, an index-interpreter        | gate with the channel allow-list refuses with                |               |\n    81\t|    | exemplar publishing decisions. `src/cljc/dao/stream/        | `:dao.stream/refused`; a gate reads the latest decision      |               |\n    82\t|    | middleware.cljc`, tests.                                   | through a capacity-1 medium after eviction; a filter cannot  |               |\n    83\t|    |                                                            | be expressed.                                                |               |\n    84\t+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\n    85\t| 2  | `dao.stream.remote` core: `mirror-step`, link, reflection, | The toy over two in-process ring buffers as the channel;     | clj cljs cljd |\n    86\t|    | remote descriptor dispatch, the protocol errors.           | `gap` from an evicting source crosses verbatim with the      |               |\n    87\t|    | `src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc`, tests.                  | source's cursor; `blocked` then `ok` on re-ask; `not-found`  |               |\n    88\t|    |                                                            | marks gone; `no-surface` does not; the descriptor answer     |               |\n    89\t|    |                                                            | carries the surface; a kept cursor from a reflection is      |               |\n    90\t|    |                                                            | accepted by the source handle.                               |               |\n    91\t+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\n    92\t| 3  | WebSocket channel composition: `ws-project` at each end;   | The toy across a socket on clj to Node, Node to clj, cljd    | clj cljs cljd |\n    93\t|    | mirror steps over accepted and dialed attachments;         | to clj; both directions serve on one channel; browser        |               |\n    94\t|    | retire `:ws/accept`, disclaim and the served-path table    | dials and reads; a closed connection is observed as the      |               |\n    95\t|    | in `dao.stream.ws`.                                        | link's `end`.                                                |               |\n    96\t+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\n    97\t| 4  | Content service: the `dao.jing.content` family (section 1) | `dao.jing.remote` tests ported and passing over the new      | clj cljs cljd |\n    98\t|    | with `serve-step`, `step`, `driver` (clj), `async`;         | module; `dao.space.index`, btree hydration, the linker M3    |               |\n    99\t|    | `dao.jing/accept-bytes!`; `dao.jing.coordinate` new         | and M4 tests unchanged in outcome; no require of             |               |\n   100\t|    | coordinate; delete `src/cljc/dao/jing/remote.cljc`,        | `dao.jing.remote` remains.                                   |               |\n   101\t|    | `remote/step.cljc`, `remote/async.cljc` and their tests.   |                                                              |               |\n   102\t+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\n   103\t| 5  | REPL as a service: `yin.repl.serve` and `connect` over     | `(connect \"daostream:ws://...\")` resolves to a remote        | clj cljs cljd |\n   104\t|    | `requests` and `answers` reflections; delete               | descriptor pair; the demo REPLs work; `yin.repl.link` serves |               |\n   105\t|    | `dao.stream.serving`, `dao.stream.rpc.ws`, the apply wire  | content through slice 4; `dao.stream.rpc` is reworked over   |               |\n   106\t|    | envelope from `dao.stream.apply`; rework or retire         | reflections or retired in the same slice, because the apply  |               |\n   107\t|    | `dao.stream.rpc`.                                          | envelope it requires is deleted here.                        |               |\n   108\t+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\n   109\t| 6  | UDP channel: `dao.stream.udp` with fragmentation keyed by  | The toy over UDP with a 48 KiB value (inside the default     | clj cljs cljd |\n   110\t|    | attachment, address, direction and id; adapters            | 64 KiB maximum); loss injection recovers by resend;          |               |\n   111\t|    | `src/clj/dao/stream/udp/jvm.clj`, `src/cljs/dao/           | oversize beyond the maximum answers `transport-error`        |               |\n   112\t|    | stream/udp/node.cljs`, `src/cljd/dao/stream/udp/dart.cljd`.| with reason `oversize`.                                      |               |\n   113\t+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\n   114\t| 7  | Pair channel and the meeting and relay conventions with    | Two peers behind a simulated restricted NAT punch; behind    | clj           |\n   115\t|    | leases: `dao.stream.remote.pair`, `dao.stream.remote.meet`;| a simulated symmetric NAT they relay; a pair whose holder    |               |\n   116\t|    | a meeting gate refuses past the pair bound.                | stops renewing answers `not-found` after duration plus       |               |\n   117\t|    |                                                            | tolerance; a reconnect within it finds the pair intact; a    |               |\n   118\t|    |                                                            | meeting peer past its bound refuses, not silences.          |               |\n   119\t+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\n   120\t| 8  | UCF facade: `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md`      | The acceptance row: a string-backed stream migrates with a   | clj cljs cljd |\n   121\t|    | 7.4.3 and 7.5.3 lift and lower through remote descriptors  | kept cursor and resumes; forced eviction yields `gap` with   |               |\n   122\t|    | with the `:dao.stream.remote/v1` cursor profile.           | the source's cursor.                                         |               |\n   123\t+----+------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+---------------+\n   124\t\n   125\tSlice 7 also proves the pair rule of the spec's 3.3: a `gap` on a pair's\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
