{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.lease.md | sed -n '90,120p;230,255p;282,298p'\"","aggregated_output":"    90\t  holder is the party the grant is delivered to.\n    91\t- **A `:policy` cause may not consist of declining to count evidence\n    92\t  received.** Eligible renewals are counted whether or not another condition\n    93\t  ends the lease.\n    94\t\n    95\t## Prohibitions\n    96\t\n    97\t- A lease may not extend retention, defer eviction, or gate history, and no\n    98\t  DaoStream operation may consult a lease.\n    99\t- No timer holds a callback and no notification marks a lapse.\n   100\t- No absolute time appears in any fact.\n   101\t- A reclaim frees the resource, never the record.\n   102\t- A holder renews from its own control flow. No machinery renews on its behalf.\n   103\t\n   104\t## Time\n   105\t\n   106\tTime reaches lease code only as data; neither judge nor holder reads a host\n   107\tclock. Both read a tick stream their composition wires. Readings on one stream\n   108\tnever decrease, and a composition persisting a ledger across a restart keeps\n   109\tits readings comparable across it.\n   110\t\n   111\tA tick-stream gap makes a pass late, not wrong; a lease-fact gap is governed\n   112\tunder *Judging with incomplete evidence*.\n   113\t\n   114\t## The judge\n   115\t\n   116\tThe judge is composed **inside the boundary that possesses the resource** and\n   117\treclaims by acting on what it itself holds; one that does not possess the\n   118\tresource is outside this contract. It concludes and reclaims in one\n   119\tinterpreter, which is not the forbidden collapse: it is the possessing host\n   120\tinterpreter performing its own act.\n   230\tfrom the resource.\n   231\t\n   232\t## Composition duties\n   233\t\n   234\tA composition that grants leases owes all of the following.\n   235\t\n   236\t- **A judging interpreter, and a runtime driving it at a declared cadence** —\n   237\t  the maximum interval between *completed* passes.\n   238\t- **A tick stream** for the judge, and one for every holder.\n   239\t- **A tolerance** supplied to the judge, possibly zero.\n   240\t- **An attribution resolver** for the judge and for every holder observing a\n   241\t  grant — its own answer to who authored a fact, by per-author media, an\n   242\t  envelope key, or a transport's attachment identity, since DaoStream supplies\n   243\t  none. One handed no resolver, or one incompatible with its medium, is refused\n   244\t  at assembly.\n   245\t- **A reclaim procedure per subject**, idempotent, reporting success.\n   246\t- **A stream the grantor writes grants and `:lapsed` to**, and the medium each\n   247\t  recipient reads its carried facts from.\n   248\t- **Media that either retain without eviction or declare evict-oldest**,\n   249\t  refused at assembly otherwise.\n   250\t- **For durable resources, three things this vocabulary does not supply**: a\n   251\t  judge whose durability matches the resource, a rule for which incarnation may\n   252\t  reclaim, and fencing from the resource. A composition that has not settled\n   253\t  all three keeps its leases process-scoped.\n   254\t\n   255\t## Sizing\n   282\t\n   283\t## Carriage\n   284\t\n   285\tProposals, grants, refusals, releases and renewals cross a boundary as ordinary\n   286\tpayload, carried by the composition to the medium the recipient reads. Carriage\n   287\tis delivery, not a second authoring.\n   288\t\n   289\t`:lapsed` does not cross; it is the grantor's record on the grantor's stream. A\n   290\tremote holder learns of a reclaim by observing it — for a served connection, an\n   291\tordinary `:ws/closed`; for a stream served under `dao.stream.remote.md`, the\n   292\t`not-found` protocol error its mirror answers for the reclaimed identity. A remote holder that\n   293\treads the grantor's stream through a served handle is observing the grantor's\n   294\trecord, not receiving carriage. No close code is assigned here; distinguishing\n   295\treclaim on the wire belongs to `dao.stream.ws.md`'s deferred close-code design.\n   296\t\n   297\t## Out of scope\n   298\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
